{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "P1-L1",
      "quote": "Implement `parse_amount(s)` so decimal text becomes integer cents."
    },
    {
      "id": "P1-L2",
      "quote": "- Accept string inputs in ordinary decimal notation with at most two fractional digits."
    },
    {
      "id": "P1-L3",
      "quote": "- Store and return every amount as an integer number of cents: `12.30` becomes 1230, `3` becomes 300, and `-2.00` becomes -200."
    },
    {
      "id": "P1-L4",
      "quote": "- **Return `None` for every malformed or non-string input.** - Do not raise an exception or print anything for invalid input."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L1",
      "quote": "Implement `parse_record(line)` to validate one record line and produce its specified dictionary."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L2",
      "quote": "- The line must have exactly five `|`-separated fields: `TYPE|RECORD_ID|ORDER_ID|AMOUNT|TIMESTAMP`."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L3",
      "quote": "- `TYPE` must be `ORDER` or `PAYMENT`, matched case-insensitively and stored uppercase."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L4",
      "quote": "- Trim both identifiers;"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L5",
      "quote": "reject the row if either is empty."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L6",
      "quote": "For an `ORDER`, `RECORD_ID` and `ORDER_ID` must be equal."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L7",
      "quote": "- Parse `AMOUNT` with `parse_amount`;"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L8",
      "quote": "a negative order is invalid, while a negative payment is a refund."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L9",
      "quote": "Amounts are integer cents."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2-L10",
      "quote": "- `TIMESTAMP` must use `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM` and be stored as a naive `datetime`."
    }
  ],
